b:T2baa,<p>This Seller Policy ("Policy") governs the participation of all sellers on <strong>Smile Agri-Market Technologies Ltd</strong> ("Smile Agri-Market," "Company," "we," "our," or "us"), including through <a href="https://smileagrimarket.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>https://smileagrimarket.com</strong></a> and our mobile applications (collectively, the "Platform").</p>
<p>By registering as a seller, listing products, or offering services on the Platform, you agree to comply with this Policy, our Terms & Conditions, Privacy Policy, and all applicable laws.</p>
<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market is committed to building a trusted, transparent, and reliable agricultural marketplace. This Policy establishes the standards all sellers must follow to protect buyers, promote fair trading, and maintain the integrity of the Platform.</p>
<h2>2. Seller Eligibility</h2>
<p>To sell on the Platform, you must:</p>
<ul><li>Be at least 18 years of age or the age of legal majority in your jurisdiction.</li><li>Have the legal authority to sell the products or services you list.</li><li>Complete any required identity or business verification.</li><li>Maintain accurate contact information.</li><li>Comply with applicable laws, regulations, and industry standards.</li></ul>
<p>Businesses may be required to provide:</p>
<ul><li>Certificate of Incorporation or Business Registration.</li><li>Tax Identification Number (TIN), where applicable.</li><li>Relevant licenses or permits.</li><li>Bank account details for payouts.</li><li>Additional documents requested during verification.</li></ul>
<h2>3. Seller Verification</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may require verification before allowing a seller to list products or receive payments.</p>
<p>Verification may include:</p>
<ul><li>Government-issued identification.</li><li>Selfie or biometric verification.</li><li>Business registration documents.</li><li>Proof of address.</li><li>Farm ownership or lease documentation.</li><li>Product certifications.</li><li>Bank account verification.</li></ul>
<p>Failure to complete verification may delay or restrict access to selling privileges.</p>
<h2>4. Product Eligibility</h2>
<p>Sellers may list only products and services that comply with applicable laws and our marketplace standards.</p>
<p>Examples include:</p>
<ul><li>Fresh fruits and vegetables.</li><li>Grains and cereals.</li><li>Livestock and poultry (where permitted).</li><li>Fish and seafood.</li><li>Farm inputs such as seeds and fertilizers.</li><li>Farm machinery and equipment.</li><li>Greenhouse materials.</li><li>Irrigation equipment.</li><li>Agricultural consulting services.</li><li>Training and educational services.</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may refuse, remove, or suspend listings that do not meet marketplace requirements.</p>
<h2>5. Prohibited Products</h2>
<p>The following may not be listed or sold through the Platform unless expressly permitted by applicable law and approved by Smile Agri-Market:</p>
<ul><li>Counterfeit goods.</li><li>Stolen property.</li><li>Expired products.</li><li>Unsafe food.</li><li>Contaminated agricultural products.</li><li>Illegal pesticides or chemicals.</li><li>Prohibited wildlife or protected species.</li><li>Products that infringe intellectual property rights.</li><li>Hazardous materials requiring licenses not held by the seller.</li><li>Fraudulent investment opportunities.</li><li>Any product prohibited by law.</li></ul>
<p>We reserve the right to remove prohibited listings immediately.</p>
<h2>6. Product Listings</h2>
<p>Sellers are responsible for ensuring that listings are:</p>
<ul><li>Accurate.</li><li>Complete.</li><li>Honest.</li><li>Up to date.</li></ul>
<p>Each listing should include, where applicable:</p>
<ul><li>Product name.</li><li>Description.</li><li>Price.</li><li>Quantity.</li><li>Unit of measurement.</li><li>Product photographs.</li><li>Harvest date or production date (where relevant).</li><li>Expiry date (where applicable).</li><li>Country or region of origin.</li><li>Delivery options.</li><li>Available inventory.</li></ul>
<p>Misleading descriptions are prohibited.</p>
<h2>7. Product Quality</h2>
<p>Sellers are responsible for ensuring that products:</p>
<ul><li>Meet applicable quality standards.</li><li>Are safe for their intended use.</li><li>Match the listing description.</li><li>Are fit for sale.</li><li>Are properly stored before dispatch.</li><li>Are packaged appropriately to minimize damage during transportation.</li></ul>
<p>Perishable products should be harvested, handled, and transported using appropriate agricultural and food safety practices.</p>
<h2>8. Pricing</h2>
<p>Sellers determine their own prices unless otherwise agreed.</p>
<p>Prices should:</p>
<ul><li>Be clear and accurate.</li><li>Include any mandatory charges where required by law.</li><li>Not contain hidden fees.</li><li>Be updated promptly when changes occur.</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market reserves the right to correct obvious pricing errors or suspend listings containing misleading pricing.</p>
<h2>9. Inventory Management</h2>
<p>Sellers are responsible for maintaining accurate inventory levels.</p>
<p>You should:</p>
<ul><li>Remove unavailable products promptly.</li><li>Update stock quantities regularly.</li><li>Avoid overselling.</li><li>Notify affected buyers immediately if inventory becomes unavailable after an order is placed.</li></ul>
<p>Repeated inventory inaccuracies may affect seller performance ratings.</p>
<h2>10. Order Fulfilment</h2>
<p>Sellers are expected to:</p>
<ul><li>Confirm orders promptly.</li><li>Prepare products carefully.</li><li>Dispatch orders within the stated processing time.</li><li>Communicate any delays as soon as reasonably possible.</li><li>Provide tracking information where available.</li></ul>
<p>Failure to fulfil accepted orders without a valid reason may result in penalties or account restrictions.</p>
<h2>11. Packaging Standards</h2>
<p>Products should be packaged to:</p>
<ul><li>Protect against damage during transportation.</li><li>Preserve freshness for perishable goods.</li><li>Prevent contamination.</li><li>Comply with applicable food safety regulations.</li><li>Include any required labels or handling instructions.</li></ul>
<h2>12. Delivery Responsibilities</h2>
<p>Where sellers arrange delivery directly, they are responsible for:</p>
<ul><li>Delivering to the correct address.</li><li>Meeting agreed delivery timelines where reasonably possible.</li><li>Using suitable transportation methods.</li><li>Providing delivery updates when available.</li></ul>
<p>If Smile Agri-Market or a third-party logistics partner is used, sellers must cooperate to ensure timely collection and dispatch.</p>
<h2>13. Seller Conduct</h2>
<p>Sellers must:</p>
<ul><li>Treat buyers respectfully.</li><li>Respond to enquiries promptly.</li><li>Honour accepted orders.</li><li>Provide accurate information.</li><li>Resolve disputes in good faith.</li><li>Comply with Platform policies.</li></ul>
<p>Abusive, discriminatory, deceptive, or threatening behaviour is prohibited.</p>
<h2>14. Payments and Payouts</h2>
<p>Payments received through the Platform may be:</p>
<ul><li>Subject to verification.</li><li>Held temporarily for fraud prevention or dispute resolution.</li><li>Reduced by applicable marketplace commissions, transaction fees, taxes, or other disclosed charges.</li></ul>
<p>Payouts will generally be made to the verified bank account provided by the seller in accordance with our payout schedule.</p>
<h2>15. Marketplace Fees</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may charge sellers fees for:</p>
<ul><li>Successful sales.</li><li>Featured listings.</li><li>Advertising.</li><li>Premium seller services.</li><li>Subscription plans.</li><li>Payment processing.</li><li>Logistics coordination.</li></ul>
<p>Applicable fees will be communicated before they are charged.</p>
<h2>16. Ratings and Reviews</h2>
<p>Buyers may rate and review sellers based on their transaction experience.</p>
<p>Sellers may not:</p>
<ul><li>Manipulate ratings.</li><li>Purchase fake reviews.</li><li>Offer incentives in exchange for positive reviews without disclosure.</li><li>Harass buyers over reviews.</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may remove reviews that violate our policies.</p>
<h2>17. Returns and Refunds</h2>
<p>Sellers must cooperate with Smile Agri-Market during investigations relating to returns or refund requests.</p>
<p>Where a refund is approved due to seller error, the seller may be responsible for:</p>
<ul><li>The refund amount.</li><li>Return shipping costs where applicable.</li><li>Any additional costs permitted under Platform policies.</li></ul>
<h2>18. Intellectual Property</h2>
<p>Sellers warrant that they own or have the necessary rights to use all product names, photographs, logos, trademarks, descriptions, and other content uploaded to the Platform.</p>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may remove content that appears to infringe the rights of others.</p>
<h2>19. Compliance with Laws</h2>
<p>Sellers are responsible for complying with all applicable laws and regulations, including those relating to:</p>
<ul><li>Food safety.</li><li>Consumer protection.</li><li>Agriculture.</li><li>Product labeling.</li><li>Environmental protection.</li><li>Taxation.</li><li>Employment.</li><li>Import and export controls, where applicable.</li></ul>
<h2>20. Suspension and Termination</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may suspend or terminate seller accounts for reasons including:</p>
<ul><li>Fraud.</li><li>Repeated customer complaints.</li><li>Failure to meet quality standards.</li><li>Sale of prohibited goods.</li><li>Repeated order cancellations.</li><li>Misrepresentation.</li><li>Failure to complete verification.</li><li>Violation of this Policy or our Terms & Conditions.</li></ul>
<p>We may also remove listings or withhold payouts where reasonably necessary to investigate suspected misconduct.</p>
<h2>21. Limitation of Liability</h2>
<p>Sellers acknowledge that Smile Agri-Market provides a marketplace platform and does not guarantee sales volumes, buyer behavior, uninterrupted access to the Platform, or the performance of third-party service providers.</p>
<p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, Smile Agri-Market shall not be liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential losses arising from a seller's use of the Platform.</p>
<h2>22. Amendments</h2>
<p>We may update this Seller Policy from time to time.</p>
<p>Material changes will be published on the Platform with an updated Effective Date. Continued use of the Platform after the effective date constitutes acceptance of the revised Policy.</p>
<h2>23. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If you have questions regarding this Seller Policy, please contact:</p>
<p><strong>Smile Agri-Market Technologies Ltd</strong></p>
<p>Website: <a href="https://smileagrimarket.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>https://smileagrimarket.com</strong></a></p>
<p>Seller Support: <a href="mailto:sellers@smileagrimarket.com"><strong>sellers@smileagrimarket.com</strong></a></p>
<p>General Support: <a href="mailto:support@smileagrimarket.com"><strong>support@smileagrimarket.com</strong></a></p>6:["$","main",null,{"className":"container-page py-12 sm:py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.7rem] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground","children":"Legal"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl","children":"Seller Policy"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":["Effective date: ","July 9, 2026"," · Last updated:"," ","July 9, 2026"]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&_a]:font-medium [&_a]:text-leaf-600 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-4 [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h3]:mt-7 [&_h3]:text-base [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-ink [&_li]:mt-2 [&_ol]:mt-4 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-6 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-ink [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$b"}}],"$Lc"]}]}]
